stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> RunningA: box running slot A (good)
  RunningA --> Staged: signed bundle verified and written to slot B
  Staged --> TrialB: reboot, slot B on trial (marker set)
  TrialB --> CommittedB: fresh-signal gate passes 3x
  TrialB --> TrialB: crash or power cut, tries left (x86 GRUB: 3)
  TrialB --> RunningA: gate timeout, watchdog, or tries used up
  RunningA --> MarkedBad: release recorded as bad (no auto-retry)
  CommittedB --> [*]: B is the new good slot, A kept as fallback
  note right of TrialB
    Pi 5 tryboot and the x86 efi route give ONE try per boot entry,
    so an interrupted trial is re-offered from the kept download
  end note
